# Where the ERP API lives.
#   local development  http://127.0.0.1:3000
#   production         https://api.ghumtibags.com   (the Cloudflare Worker)
ERP_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# Exactly one of the following. Neither is NEXT_PUBLIC_: these are read only in
# server components and route handlers, so they never reach a browser bundle.
#
# Talking to the Worker (production) — its edge gate expects this header:
# ERP_CLIENT_API_KEY=

# Talking to the Rust origin directly (local development, no Worker in front) —
# same value as the server's API_KEY:
ERP_ORIGIN_API_KEY=

# The storefront's own public origin, used for canonical URLs, Open Graph images
# and sitemap entries. Must be set in production — a sitemap full of localhost
# URLs is worse than none.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key, pairing with the ERP's TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY.
# Guards checkout and the sign-in code request.
#
# Required in production: `next start` refuses to boot without it (see
# src/instrumentation.ts), and the ERP should run with TURNSTILE_REQUIRED=true.
# It is inlined at build time, so set it where the deployed build is made — a
# key added only at runtime does not reach the widget.
#
# Unset in development renders no widget and submits no token; the ERP skips the
# check when it has no secret either. `next build` succeeds without it, so CI
# needs no key.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
